---
description: Project-wide Technical Debt Intelligence & Governance PoC principles
alwaysApply: true
---

- `Signal`, `Candidate`, and `TechnicalDebt` are distinct lifecycle concepts.
- A signal is not automatically technical debt.
- Multiple evidence items may support one structural technical-debt candidate.
- AI provides recommendations; evidence explains; authorized humans make critical lifecycle decisions.
- Do not allow AI to validate, accept risk, or close technical debt.
- Prefer clear code over clever code.
- Do not introduce unnecessary abstractions.
- Do not implement functionality outside the current task scope.
- Do not refactor unrelated files.
- Do not hard-code secrets, infrastructure-specific connection information, or model/provider identifiers.
- Do not implement frontend code until the frontend technology decision is explicitly made.
